course: dictionary
lesson: 13019
title: Eyelets: small holes with a job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eyelet is a small round hole in cloth, leather or paper. A lace, string or hook goes through it. You can find eyelets on trainers, tents, banners and curtains. «Mum threaded the lace through the eyelets of my trainers.» The lace goes in and out of the holes to hold the shoe closed.
explain: Sometimes an eyelet is also a small metal ring. The ring makes the hole stronger, so it does not tear. «The tent has metal eyelets so the ropes can be tied to the pegs.» Here the eyelets are the strong metal rings around the holes.
explain: Read the words around eyelet to find its meaning. Ask yourself: what goes through it? What is it on? In «The banner had neat eyelets along the top», the banner hangs from those holes, so an eyelet is a hole that something can hang from.
fact: An eyelet is a small round hole in cloth, leather or paper.
fact: A lace, string or hook goes through an eyelet.
fact: «Eyelet» can also mean the small metal ring that strengthens the hole.
fact: Eyelets are found on shoes, trainers, tents, banners and curtains.
fact: In design and technology, you may add metal eyelets to strengthen a hole in paper or cloth.
exercise: «Mum threaded the lace through the eyelets of my trainers.» What is an eyelet? | A loud noise | A type of shoe | A long piece of string | *A small round hole that a lace goes through
exercise: «The sail had metal eyelets at the corners so the rope could be tied on tightly.» What do the metal eyelets most likely do? | Change the colour of the sail | Make the sail heavier and slower | Hold the sail up in the sky | *Strengthen the holes so the rope does not tear them
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a small round hole: «The banner had neat eyelets along the top.» | *eyelets | banner | along | neat
test: «Each eyelet on the tent was reinforced with metal.» What is an eyelet in this sentence? | A window in the roof | A peg that holds the tent down | A thick rope for tying | *A small hole, strengthened with a metal ring
test: Which of these would NOT usually have eyelets? | *A trainer | A banner | A tent | A cloud in the sky
exam: «Ali added a metal eyelet to the paper bag so the string would not tear the paper.» What does eyelet mean? | A tool for cutting paper | *A small round hole, often strengthened with a metal ring | A kind of paper bag with a handle | A bright coloured string
